From: Marco Martins <marcomartins86@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] MIPS: kexec: sync the instruction cache with the copied kernel

machine_kexec() flushes the caches and then calls kexec_reboot(), which
still runs set_cpu_online() and local_flush_icache_range() before it
jumps to the relocation code, so their lines stay valid in the
instruction cache. The relocation code copies the new kernel over the
old one and jumps to it without touching the caches (except on Octeon),
so where both kernels have code at the same address the new kernel can
run stale lines of the old one. It calls set_cpu_online() itself in
boot_cpu_init(), before it prints anything, and hangs there when its
copy sits at a different address than the old kernel's.

On R2 and later, write each copied page back from the data cache and
drop it from the instruction cache with SYNCI, and jump to the new
kernel with JR.HB.

Signed-off-by: Marco Martins <marcomartins86@gmail.com>
---
--- a/arch/mips/kernel/relocate_kernel.S
+++ b/arch/mips/kernel/relocate_kernel.S
@@ -65,8 +65,21 @@
 	PTR_ADDIU	s4, s4, SZREG
 	PTR_ADDIU	s2, s2, SZREG
 	LONG_ADDIU	s6, s6, -1
-	beq		s6, zero, process_entry
+	beq		s6, zero, 2f
 	b		copy_word
+2:
+#if MIPS_ISA_REV >= 2
+	/* the old kernel's code may still be cached at the page's address */
+	rdhwr		t0, $1
+	beqz		t0, process_entry
+	li		t1, (1 << _PAGE_SHIFT)
+	PTR_SUBU	t1, s4, t1
+3:	synci		0(t1)
+	PTR_ADDU	t1, t1, t0
+	sltu		t2, t1, s4
+	bnez		t2, 3b
+#endif
+	b		process_entry
 
 done:
 #ifdef CONFIG_SMP
@@ -97,7 +110,11 @@
 	sync
 #endif
 	/* jump to kexec_start_address */
+#if MIPS_ISA_REV >= 2
+	jr.hb		s1
+#else
 	j		s1
+#endif
 	END(kexec_relocate_new_kernel)
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_SMP
